EXT. FISHING TRAWLER "NORTHERN STAR" - NIGHT

Black water. A creaking hull. Fog.

INT. TRAWLER - GALLEY - CONTINUOUS

CLOSE ON a sat-phone on the table, its green light blinking. Beside it, JONAH (20s) lies on a bench, shirt soaked red at the ribs.

NELL (30s, oilskins, shaking hands) presses a rag to the wound. HALE (60s, the captain) stands in the doorway, staring at the ceiling.

NELL
Stay with me, Jonah. Cap, get Dr. Sun on that thing.

HALE
Line's open.

Nell grabs the phone, thumb-hits speaker.

DR. SUN (V.O.)
(crackling)
Nell? I can barely hear you. Is the bleeding steady?

NELL
Steady-ish. It's deep. Pete's the only one who's done this before.

ANGLE ON the hatch. PETE (50s, grey beard) is on the ladder, face white, hands empty.

PETE
I can't, Nell. I told you. I can't do it again.

DR. SUN (V.O.)
Pete. Listen to me. You can.

A heavy THUMP from above. Something drags across the deck.

Everyone looks up.

HALE
That wasn't the nets.

WE SEE the hatch. Bolted. Shaking.

BACK TO SCENE:

Jonah grips Nell's wrist.

JONAH
Nell... something's out there.

The lights die.
